# MCP server documentation

`MCP.md` at the repository root is the public catalog of Favlo’s `POST /mcp` tools and `favlo://` resources.

When you add, remove, or rename a tool or resource, change tool parameters or defaults, change optional-task behavior, or change what generate tools return (links, inline media, task fields), update `MCP.md` in the same change.

`docs/serve.md` stays the listener note: transport, queue, preemption, logging, and client wiring. Do not duplicate the full tool tables there; add or adjust a single pointer to `MCP.md` if the serve note still names tools inline.

Do not document chat completion or OpenAI HTTP routes in `MCP.md`. Do not add HTTP `/v1/images`, `/v1/videos`, or `/v1/audio` routes to satisfy MCP clients.

Follow [documentation.mdc](documentation.mdc) for tone and placeholders.

## Tool description length

The MCP specification does not cap `tools/list` description length. OpenAI Chat Completions rejects `tools[].function.description` above 1024 characters. Favlo keeps every mounted tool description at or under `TOOL_DESCRIPTION_MAX_CHARS` (**256**) in `src/favlo/mcp_server.py`. A pipeline tool is not added to `MCP.md`.

Each parameter `description` in that tool's JSON Schema stays at or under `TOOL_PARAM_DESCRIPTION_MAX_CHARS` (**48**). Prefer an empty property description when the name and type are enough. Put long routing guidance in standing instructions, not in tool or parameter descriptions.

When you change a listener tool docstring, an Args line, an explicit `description=`, or memory tool copy, run:

```bash
uv run pytest tests/test_mcp_tool_descriptions.py -q
```

That suite must stay green.
